  "spec_element": "invariant",
  "proof_obligation": "preservation",
  "diagnosis": "The second loop invariant is stated as forall b :: 0 <= b <= (n) - 1 ==> Sum(a, b, n) <= Sum(a, c, n), which only quantifies over b up to n-1. After the loop body executes (t += a[n], n := n+1), the new invariant must hold for b up to the new n-1 = old_n. For b = old_n, we need Sum(a, old_n, new_n) = a[old_n] <= Sum(a, c, new_n) = old_t + a[old_n], which requires old_t >= 0. The old invariant with bound n-1 does not provide Sum(a, old_n, old_n) = 0 <= old_t to establish this. By extending the bound to include b = n, the invariant guarantees Sum(a, n, n) = 0 <= Sum(a, c, n) (i.e., t >= 0), which is exactly what is needed to show preservation when t >= 0, and in the t < 0 reset case the strengthened bound is also sufficient.",
  "repair": "invariant forall b :: 0 <= b <= n ==> Sum(a, b, n) <= Sum(a, c, n)"
}
